        "Abstract": "Research in task-oriented dialog has been, for a long time, limited by the existence of only monolingual English datasets. We introduce mz, a multilingual, multi-domain task-oriented dialog dataset in four languages (Arabic, Chinese, German, and Russian), created by translating the English MultiWOZ 2.1 dataset. We present extensive experiments on zero-shot and few-shot cross-lingual transfer for dialog state tracking (DST) and response retrieval (RR), demonstrating that intermediate conversational specialization for the target language substantially improves the sample efficiency in the downstream few-shot transfer."
